From f3c3c34a72012edd6c6c872ce9ae44044f008f64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:56:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): a stop or go-home asked after a live-tool section
 posts at the end of that section

fanuc-lathe.cps's section end returned from its C-axis live-tool branch
before afterOp(), so an optional stop (M01), program stop (M00) or go-home
asked after a cross drill or C-axis milling op was not posted there and
the pending ask came out after the NEXT section instead.

Every section now ends with its own ask: the live branch releases the
live spindle (live_tool.spindle_off), then the C axis (c_axis_off),
restores G99, then afterOp() writes the stop or the X-then-Z home - the
turning branch's order with the live section's own release words in the
spindle-stop place. A refused live section still consumes its ask.

Pinned by script_fanuc_lathe's after-live tests (M01, M00, go-home, and
no stop asked) and the new live_then_stop recorded case with goldens in
every per-post script suite. No existing golden changes.

Fixes #1188

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
